# The summariser's harness.
#
# An instrument, not a station. A station moves the work forward and the commit
# would differ without it; delete this one and the commit is byte-identical. All
# it does is read what the line already wrote and say it shorter.
#
# `--no-tools` is what makes that a fact rather than a claim. It has no read, no
# edit, no shell, no way to reach the repository at all. It sees the text it is
# handed and nothing else, which is the whole of what it needs, and means an
# instrument can never become a station by accident.
#
# Haiku because compressing two paragraphs into a sentence is not the hard part
# of this line, and it happens between every station a human is waiting on.
TOOLS=""
MODEL="anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5"
